# 18. Risks and Development Challenges

## 18.1 Maze Navigation

Large mazes can become confusing or frustrating.

**Proposed solution:** Design clear visual landmarks, useful navigation systems and multiple route options.

## 18.2 Mobile Performance

Large 3D environments can place significant demands on mobile hardware.

**Proposed solution:** Optimise rendering, textures, lighting and environmental detail.

## 18.3 Multiplayer Networking

Synchronising players, weapons, movement and combat can be technically challenging.

**Proposed solution:** Prototype networking early and test under realistic conditions.

## 18.4 Combat Balance

Some weapons may become too powerful in narrow corridors.

**Proposed solution:** Balance weapons against different maze environments and combat distances.

## 18.5 Match Pacing

Players may spend too long searching without encountering opponents.

**Proposed solution:** Use map design, objectives, match timers and carefully tested player placement to maintain engagement.

## 18.6 Player Frustration

Players may repeatedly become trapped or lost.

**Proposed solution:** Make navigation challenging but understandable, and provide enough environmental information for players to learn the map.

